  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame illuminated">
      <p class="lede">The density toward zero was always asserted. Now it is built: it is where the
        returners pile, turn after turn, forever short of the ground.</p>
      <h3 id="t-two-densities">15.3 &mdash; two densities, kept apart</h3>
      <p>The chapter is careful where it would be easy to cheat. <strong>Population density</strong>
        &mdash; how many beings occupy the small region &mdash; is what the returners produce, and the
        mechanism owns it completely: every fork at every level sends someone downward, so the low region
        receives traffic from all densities above it. <strong>Numerical density</strong> &mdash; how many
        numbers occupy a region &mdash; is Cantor's, a property of the value system and nothing to do
        with beings. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
      <p>The new idea is the <em>conjecture</em> that the two coincide: that the beings pile where the
        numbers crowd, and that the foundational density is the shadow of the fork's returns. It is named
        as a conjecture in the text and is named as one here. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

